    "note": "Senate Draft 2 (SD2). Subsection (c) of 134-8 is amended to drop \"designed for or capable of use with a pistol\" and to exempt magazines legally possessed before the Act; it mixes struck and new words, so it is not quoted. Violating (c) is a misdemeanor, a class C felony if the magazine is inserted in a firearm. The bill has a Senate passage vote (23-2); amendments made after the version read are not in the text read."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 2 (HRS 134-8): (d) No person shall sell, barter, trade, gift, transfer, or acquire, except by means of inheritance, a detachable ammunition magazine pursuant to this subsection. (e) Detachable ammunition magazines with a capacity in excess of ten rounds may be acquired, possessed, and used by a law enforcement agency or duly authorized law enforcement officer for official purposes."
